	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Patients were required to have a qualifying thin-section inspiratory CT near CLAD diagnosis, and cases with failed segmentation were excluded, which is most consistent with complete-case/exclusion-based handling. Preprocessing was described in detail: lung segmentation, removal of large airways/central vasculature, voxel texture assignment, radiologist review of overlays, and normalization of ML variables by CT total lung capacity. No class-imbalance method, code release, or train/test split was reported because this was not a new model-training study in this cohort.  ￼

